ps a knight to a natural square, increases pressure on the center (especially e4), and does not commit to a specific pawn structure yet. It also avoids symmetry, potentially provoking imbalances. While e7-e5 is tempting, playing the knight first allows me to wait and see how White proceeds in the center before locking in my pawn moves.\n\nAnswer: N: g8-f6'}
