ng moves are passive and waste tempo when a promotion is available.\n- **R: g8-h8/g8-f8/g8-e8**: Rook moves don’t address the urgency of promoting and lose time.\n- **P: f4-e3**: Capturing on e3 wins a bishop, but ignores the free promotion — objectively worse than queening.\n- **P: b6-b5/g7-g6/h7-h6**: Pawn pushes on the kingside or queenside are slow and neglect the critical b2-b1 threat.\n\nReason: The pawn on b2 must promote immediately. Delaying it loses a winning advantage. Promoting to queen gives the strongest follow-up — it could support an attack, defend against threats, or dominate the board. There is no risk of stalemate, and White cannot stop the promotion. Thus, queening is optimal.\n\nAnswer: P: b2-b1-q'}
