awn on the kingside, but it's far from promotion and doesn’t address the king’s vulnerability.\n\nBest options:\n- K: c7-c8 – consolidates the king toward the corner, potentially preparing rook activity and avoiding central exposure.\n- R: b8-c8 – doubles on the c-file with the king, offering protection and coordination.\n\nHowever, **K: c7-c8** places the king in a slightly safer corner and frees the b8-rook to operate without being pinned to king defense. It also avoids blocking potential rook checks on the c-file.\n\nReason: Centralizing or retreating the king to c8 improves safety and allows flexible coordination with the rook. While rook moves are tempting, the king’s vulnerability takes priority. c8 is safer than d6/d7/d8.\n\nAnswer: K: c7-c8"}
