 — legal for a queen.  \n  - After Qe8+, white king on f6 is in check.  \n  - Possible escapes: f6-f7? But f7 is occupied by black pawn (PBF0). f6-g6? No. f6-f5? Still attacked by queen. f6-e6? Also covered by queen on e8. So **Qe8 is checkmate**.\n\nThus, Q: e4-e8 is not just a good move — it is checkmate.\n\nReason: Delivering checkmate ends the game immediately. Among all valid moves, Q: e4-e8 achieves this. It exploits the exposed position of the white king on f6, which is aligned on the same file as the black queen and has no flight squares or defenders.\n\nAnswer: Q: e4-e8"}
