: d8-c7 – Activates king, supports future b-pawn promotion.\n3. R: b8-c8 – Could double pressure on c-file after pawn capture.\n\nReason: Capturing the pawn on c6 with P: b7-c6 gains material and weakens White’s structure. After this, Black will have two connected passed pawns on the queenside (b6 and c6), while White’s king is exposed. This creates strong winning chances in the endgame. Delaying the capture risks White reorganizing. Therefore, capturing immediately is optimal.\n\nAnswer: P: b7-c6'}
