ior to any passive move.\n\nWhy wasn't this obvious earlier? Because the king is on g4 and rook moves to f4 attack it directly.\n\nSo **R: f5-f4** is a winning move — it checks the enemy king.\n\nReason: This move delivers check to the White king on g4, forcing it into a difficult position with limited escape squares, increasing pressure and likely leading to material gain or mating attack. It’s the most forcing and strongest move on the board.\n\nAnswer: R: f5-f4"}
