\n1 |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    | 1\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n     a    b    c    d    e    f    g    h \nYour valid moves are (src-dst-promotion, or src-dst):\n[P: b5-b4, K: c4-b3, K: c4-b4, K: c4-c3, K: c4-c5, K: c4-d3, K: c4-d4, K: c4-d5, Q: h3-g2, Q: h3-f1, Q: h3-g3, Q: h3-f3, Q: h3-e3, Q: h3-d3, Q: h3-c3, Q: h3-b3, Q: h3-a3, Q: h3-g4, Q: h3-f5, Q: h3-e6, Q: h3-d7, Q: h3-c8, Q: h3-h2, Q: h3-h1, Q: h3-h4, Q: h3-h5, Q: h3-h6, Q: h3-h7, Q: h3-h8]\nYour answer format should be: Answer: piece-name: move. \nPiece-name and move (src-dst-promotion or src-dst) should be directly copied EXACTLY from valid move list.\nExample of valid output format: N: a1-b3; P: e7-e8-q; Piece B: g5-f4.\nPlease select a move from your valid moves that maximize your probability of winning.\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': "Situation: The position is highly unusual and nearly empty. Black has only three pieces left: a king on c4, a pawn on b5, and a queen on h3. White has just a king on g5 and a pawn on f7 (though not directly visible in the piece list, its presence is implied by the board state). However, based on the provided board representation, only Black’s pieces and one White king are present — it appears White may only have the king on g5. The Black king is centrally exposed but not currently in check. The Black queen is on h3, with wide-ranging mobility along ranks, files, and diagonals. The Black pawn on b5 is advanced but isolated.\n\nNotably, there is a White king on g5 (KWF1), which is very far advanced — likely a result of an unusual game. The Black king is on c4, quite distant from the action, while the Black queen has excellent activity potential.\n\nEvaluation:\n- **P: b5-b4**: Pushes the pawn, but this doesn’t contribute to immediate threats or safety. It loses a tempo and doesn’t pressure White.\n- **K: c4-b3, c4-b4, c4-c3, c4-d3, etc.**: King moves are mostly slow and don’t create threats. The king is not under threat, so moving it now is low