ol the 6th or 7th rank horizontally might also help, such as **Q: e8-d7** or **Q: e8-f7**, but d7 and f7 are adjacent to g7, risking allowing the White king to capture if not careful — though currently not possible since they're not moving into attack range without consequence.\n- **Q: e8-e5** or **e8-e4** are too passive.\n- Best strategy: Use the queen to limit king movement while bringing the Black king (c5) closer over time.\n\nBest immediate move: **Q: e8-e2** — this places the queen on the same file as the White king, two squares away, cutting off retreat and preparing for a ladder-style checkmate with support from the Black king.\n\nReason: Q: e8-e2 maximally restricts the White king’s mobility, controls the entire e-file, and sets up a classic queen + king checkmating pattern. It forces the White king toward the edge (likely h-file or 1st/8th rank), where mate can be delivered in coordination with the advancing Black king.\n\nAnswer: Q: e8-e2"}
